================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS (Record)
================================================================================

1. **Navigation Pattern**: All CTAs use semantic <a> tags, not JS navigation
   - Rationale: Progressive enhancement, SEO, accessibility
   - Future: Can enhance with prefetching if needed

2. **Card Link Strategy**: Wrap entire card, not just title
   - Rationale: Larger touch target, better UX
   - Exception: Add to Cart button (future feature)

3. **ARIA Defaults**: Hardcoded English labels with prop override
   - Rationale: i18n not currently required
   - Future: Add i18n context when localization needed

4. **Mobile Spacing**: mb-8 between consecutive spotlights
   - Rationale: Visual separation without changing section rhythm
   - Alternative Considered: Internal section margin (rejected: affects desktop)

================================================================================
RISKS & MITIGATION
================================================================================

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|--------|------------|
| Copy delays | High | Medium | Sprint 3.3 isolated, won't block 3.1/3.2 |
| Responsive regression | Medium | High | Comprehensive breakpoint testing in 3.4 |
| Link routing issues | Low | High | Test all slugs against actual Sanity data |
| Accessibility gaps | Medium | Medium | Screen reader testing in 3.4 |

================================================================================
SPRINT COMPLETION CRITERIA
================================================================================

**Definition of Done**:
1. All navigation CTAs functional and verified
2. ARIA labels present and tested
3. Mobile spacing implemented
4. Cross-browser testing passed
5. No console errors
6. Lighthouse score maintained (90+ performance)

**Sign-off Required**:
- [ ] UX: Navigation flow verified
- [ ] A11y: Screen reader testing complete
- [ ] Visual: Design system compliance
- [ ] QA: Cross-browser regression testing
